From fab4092b603cbec580738a9fb572359e35c438fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mimi1337 <mimi1337@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:28:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: in-app browser panel

Adds a compact browser inside AyuGram Desktop, built on the WebView
backend that is already used by the IV/markup editor, so no new
dependency or engine is required.

* ayu/features/browser: an RpWidget panel with a small toolbar
  (back / forward / reload / address field / close) and a native
  WebView under it. The panel is attached inside the chat window,
  so it never spawns a separate OS window.
* Entry points: a compact icon in the chat top bar and an
  "Open browser" item in the main menu, shown only when the
  platform actually has a working WebView backend.
* Per-window panel instance, browsing state survives hiding.
* New ayu styles and three localization keys.

Written against the dev branch of AyuGramDesktop (browser widgets
are plain RpWidgets, WebView lifetime is owned by the panel).
